IMPORT prelude

-- Lease Agreements for Retail Premises Act 2023 (Singapore) -- which shop leases the Act covers (s 2(1) "qualifying lease" and
-- "retail premises", s 2(5), s 35(1), First and Second Schedules), what counts as non-compliance with a leasing principle
-- (s 2(2)-(4), s 6(1), (5)), the late or missing declaration of a permitted deviation (s 6(2)-(4), repeated in ss 23(3)-(5) and
-- 24(3)-(5)), and the complaint route: who may complain (s 9(1)), who may act (s 10(4)), who may escalate to adjudication (s 12(1)),
-- fee-shifting (s 14), confidentiality of mediation (ss 17, 18(1)), when a determination binds (s 25(6)), recording a settlement as
-- an order of court (s 26) and setting aside a determination (s 27(4), (6)).
--
-- Edition: Act 28 of 2023, informal consolidation, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/LARPA2023.txt. Every page is
-- footed "Informal Consolidation - version in force from 1/2/2024"; no amending Act or subsidiary legislation is annotated in the
-- text. The deposit's metadata says "Current version as at 01 Oct 2026". The date Part 3 commenced is NOT stated in the text
-- (s 1 leaves commencement to Gazette notification), so it is an input here, not a date.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Chosen for its everyday-life relevance: anyone renting a shop, salon, clinic, food outlet or other retail unit in
-- Singapore on a lease of a year or more meets it. SCOPED to coverage, non-compliance, deviations and the dispute route. Not
-- encoded: the Fair Tenancy Industry Committee (ss 3, 4), publication of the Code (s 5), the register (s 7), disclosure of
-- declarations (s 8), filing formalities (s 9(2)-(4)), the ADR body's duties (s 10(1)-(3)), mediator and adjudicator conduct
-- (ss 11, 12(3)), stays (s 13), immunities (s 15), adjudication communications (ss 21, 22), admissibility (ss 19, 20), the
-- adjudicator's procedural powers (s 25(1)-(3)), the court's powers on setting aside (s 27(7), (8)), and Part 5 save s 35(1).
-- THE LEASING PRINCIPLES THEMSELVES ARE IN THE CODE OF CONDUCT, WHICH IS NOT IN THE DEPOSIT: which matters are mandatory, which
-- deviations are permitted and which need a declaration are inputs here.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Lease Agreements for Retail Premises Act 2023 -- leases and disputes`

§§ `2(1), Second Schedule -- retail premises`

-- s 2(1): "retail premises" means "any premises in Singapore specified in the Second Schedule".
-- Second Schedule para 1: premises "used primarily" for (a) "the sale of goods by way of retail" or (b) "the supply of services".
-- Para 2: premises under para 1(b) are NOT retail premises "if they are used primarily for the purpose of conducting administrative
-- work in connection with the supply of services".
DECLARE PrimaryUse IS ONE OF
    `selling goods by retail`
    `supplying services`
    `administrative work for supplying services`
    `wholesale or storage`
    `manufacturing`

GIVEN `in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN, `the use` IS A PrimaryUse
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the premises are retail premises` IF
    `in Singapore` AND
    CONSIDER `the use`
    WHEN `selling goods by retail` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `supplying services` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `2(1), 2(5), 35(1), First Schedule -- qualifying lease`

-- s 2(1): "qualifying lease" means a lease for retail premises, or an extension or a renewal, where (a) the agreement "is signed on
-- or after the date of commencement of Part 3" and (b) the period "is or exceeds the period specified in the First Schedule",
-- "whether or not the lease ... is expressed to be governed by the law of Singapore". "lease" includes a licence, a sub-lease and a
-- sub-licence.
-- First Schedule: the period is ONE YEAR; any period for which the lease "may be extended or renewed ... is to be disregarded".
-- Illustration: 6 months with options of 6 months each is not a qualifying lease, nor is each renewal.
-- s 2(5): each extension or renewal "is treated ... as if it were in and of itself a separate lease".
-- s 35(1): the Act does not apply to an extension or renewal if (a) the original lease was signed before Part 3 commenced, (b) the
-- extension terms were agreed when the original was signed, and (c) those terms "remain unchanged".
-- The period is taken here in whole months, one year being 12 months (an inference about units only).
DECLARE Lease HAS
    `the premises are in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the primary use` IS A PrimaryUse
    `signed on or after Part 3 commenced` IS A BOOLEAN
    `months of term, ignoring options` IS A NUMBER
    `is an extension or renewal` IS A BOOLEAN
    `original lease signed before Part 3 commenced` IS A BOOLEAN
    `extension terms were agreed in the original lease` IS A BOOLEAN
    `extension terms remain unchanged` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the lease` IS A Lease
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the lease is a qualifying lease` IF
        `the premises are retail premises` (`the lease`'s `the premises are in Singapore`) (`the lease`'s `the primary use`)
    AND `the lease`'s `signed on or after Part 3 commenced`
    AND `the lease`'s `months of term, ignoring options` >= 12

GIVEN `the lease` IS A Lease
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the transitional carve-out applies` IF
        `the lease`'s `is an extension or renewal`
    AND `the lease`'s `original lease signed before Part 3 commenced`
    AND `the lease`'s `extension terms were agreed in the original lease`
    AND `the lease`'s `extension terms remain unchanged`

GIVEN `the lease` IS A Lease
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Act applies to the lease` IF
    `the lease is a qualifying lease` `the lease` AND (NOT `the transitional carve-out applies` `the lease`)

§§ `2(2)-(4), 6(1), 6(5) -- non-compliance with a leasing principle`

-- s 6(1): landlord AND tenant "must ensure that the lease agreement ... complies with the leasing principles in force at the time
-- the lease agreement is signed". s 6(5): a principle inconsistent with written law or rule of law is outside s 6(1).
-- s 2(2), (3): a permitted deviation is a mandatory matter left out, or a forbidden matter put in, "with the agreement of the
-- landlord and tenant" where the principle allows it.
-- s 2(4): non-compliance occurs where (a) a mandatory matter is not included, unless a permitted deviation; (b) a forbidden matter
-- is included, unless a permitted deviation; (c) a mandatory matter is included but "not complied with"; (d) a permitted deviation
-- included in the agreement "is not complied with".
GIVEN `the Act applies` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the principle is consistent with written law` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the principle requires the matter to be included` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the matter is in the agreement` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `it is an agreed permitted deviation` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the matter is complied with` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `there is non-compliance with the leasing principle` IF
        `the Act applies`
    AND `the principle is consistent with written law`
    AND (    (`the principle requires the matter to be included` AND (NOT `the matter is in the agreement`) AND (NOT `it is an agreed permitted deviation`))
         OR  ((NOT `the principle requires the matter to be included`) AND `the matter is in the agreement` AND (NOT `it is an agreed permitted deviation`))
         OR  (`the principle requires the matter to be included` AND `the matter is in the agreement` AND (NOT `the matter is complied with`))
         OR  (`it is an agreed permitted deviation` AND `the matter is in the agreement` AND (NOT `the matter is complied with`)))

§§ `6(2)-(4), 23(3)-(5), 24(3)-(5) -- declaring a permitted deviation`

-- s 6(2): the LANDLORD must, "if required by the leasing principle in question", submit a declaration of permitted deviation;
-- (3) within the period prescribed by the Regulations, with the fee. (4) If the landlord fails: "(a) the permitted deviation is void
-- (but not if the permitted deviation relates to a rental formula)"; and (b) any consequence the principle provides "may be
-- enforced as if it were a term of the lease agreement". The same words recur for a variation by mediated settlement (s 23(3)-(5))
-- and by settlement in adjudication (s 24(3)-(5)).
GIVEN `the principle requires a declaration` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the landlord declared in time with the fee` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the deviation relates to a rental formula` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the permitted deviation is void` IF
        `the principle requires a declaration`
    AND (NOT `the landlord declared in time with the fee`)
    AND (NOT `the deviation relates to a rental formula`)

§§ `9(1), 10(4), 12(1) -- complaining, mediating, escalating`

-- s 9(1): "A landlord or a tenant under a qualifying lease may file ... a complaint" of non-compliance.
-- s 11(1): on receipt, the body "must appoint a mediator". s 12(1): if mediation "does not result in a settlement agreement", "the
-- party that filed the complaint" may apply for an adjudicator, and the body "must so appoint"; (2) within the prescribed or
-- specified period.
-- s 10(4): an individual may be on both panels but, for any complaint, may act "either as a mediator or as an adjudicator, and not as
-- both".
DECLARE Person IS ONE OF
    `the landlord`
    `the tenant`
    `a guarantor of the tenant`
    `a neighbouring tenant`

GIVEN `who` IS A Person, `under a qualifying lease` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `may file a complaint of non-compliance` IF
    `under a qualifying lease` AND
    CONSIDER `who`
    WHEN `the landlord` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the tenant` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `filed the complaint` IS A BOOLEAN, `mediation produced a settlement` IS A BOOLEAN, `applied within the period` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `may apply for an adjudicator` IF
    `filed the complaint` AND (NOT `mediation produced a settlement`) AND `applied within the period`

GIVEN `on the panel of adjudicators` IS A BOOLEAN, `was the mediator on this complaint` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `may be appointed adjudicator on this complaint` IF
    `on the panel of adjudicators` AND (NOT `was the mediator on this complaint`)

§§ `14 -- shifting the fees`

-- s 14: an adjudicator may determine that party B pay party A some or all of A's fees if satisfied (a) the fees "are occasioned by
-- any frivolous or vexatious conduct of, or unfounded submissions by, B"; or (b) "it is fair in all the circumstances".
GIVEN `B was frivolous, vexatious or unfounded` IS A BOOLEAN, `it is fair in all the circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the adjudicator may make B pay A's fees` IF
    `B was frivolous, vexatious or unfounded` OR `it is fair in all the circumstances`

§§ `17, 18(1) -- telling others what was said in mediation`

-- s 17(1): "a person must not disclose any mediation communication to a third party". (2): where the complaint goes on to
-- adjudication, "the mediator must not disclose to the adjudicator" any mediation communication. s 18(1): disclosure is permitted
-- "Despite section 17(1) but subject to section 17(2)" with the consent of all parties (and of the maker, if not a party), for
-- anonymised research, evaluation or education, for legal advice, under a court order or written law, and in other listed cases.
-- Consent of every party therefore does not free the mediator to brief the adjudicator.
DECLARE DisclosureReason IS ONE OF
    `with the consent of all parties and the maker`
    `for anonymised research or education`
    `to seek legal advice`
    `under an order of court`
    `to tell the press`
    `to warn other tenants`

GIVEN `the reason` IS A DisclosureReason, `the mediator is telling the adjudicator` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the mediation communication may be disclosed` IF
    (NOT `the mediator is telling the adjudicator`) AND
    CONSIDER `the reason`
    WHEN `to tell the press` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `to warn other tenants` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `25(6) -- when a determination binds`

-- s 25(6): the determination "is binding on the parties and on any person claiming through or under them, unless or until" (a) the
-- court refuses permission to enforce it under s 27; (b) the dispute "is finally determined by a court or an arbitral tribunal or at
-- any other dispute resolution proceeding"; or (c) "the dispute is settled by agreement of the parties".
GIVEN `the court refused permission to enforce` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `a court or tribunal finally determined the dispute` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the parties settled` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the determination binds the parties` IF
        (NOT `the court refused permission to enforce`)
    AND (NOT `a court or tribunal finally determined the dispute`)
    AND (NOT `the parties settled`)

§§ `26 -- recording a settlement as an order of court`

-- s 26(1): a party may apply "for which no proceedings have been commenced in a court, with the consent of all the other parties".
-- (3): the court may record it if (a) "in writing and signed by or on behalf of all the parties" and (b) it contains any prescribed
-- information. (4): the court may refuse if (a) void or voidable for incapacity, fraud, misrepresentation, duress, coercion, mistake
-- or other ground; (b) a term is not capable of enforcement as an order; (c) recording "is contrary to public policy".
GIVEN `court proceedings already commenced` IS A BOOLEAN, `all other parties consent` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `may apply to record the settlement` IF
    (NOT `court proceedings already commenced`) AND `all other parties consent`

GIVEN `in writing and signed by all` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `contains the prescribed information` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `void or voidable` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `a term is unenforceable as an order` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `contrary to public policy` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the court may record it without a ground to refuse` IF
        `in writing and signed by all`
    AND `contains the prescribed information`
    AND (NOT `void or voidable`)
    AND (NOT `a term is unenforceable as an order`)
    AND (NOT `contrary to public policy`)

§§ `27(4), 27(6) -- setting a determination aside`

-- s 27(4): a party may commence proceedings in the General Division of the High Court to set aside a determination, "but that party
-- must pay into court as security the unpaid portion of the amount that that party is required to pay under the adjudication
-- determination (if any)".
-- (6): a party that was the RESPONDENT may not rely on "any ground that the party did not raise as a response" unless (a) the
-- circumstances "only arose after" the response was lodged, or (b) the party "could not reasonably have known" of them then.
GIVEN `the unpaid amount under the determination` IS A NUMBER, `the amount paid into court` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the security condition is met` IF
    `the amount paid into court` >= `the unpaid amount under the determination`

GIVEN `was the respondent` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `raised the ground in the response` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the circumstances arose after the response` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `could not reasonably have known then` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `may rely on the ground to set aside` IF
        (NOT `was the respondent`)
    OR  `raised the ground in the response`
    OR  `the circumstances arose after the response`
    OR  `could not reasonably have known then`
